+        // its exact bytes in buffer/texture blits yet return different U/V
+        // texels to a shader sampling an in-place RG16Unorm image alias.
+        //
+        // Measured with the Sequoia Sunrise 3840x2160 x420 video: 12 decoded
+        // frames had correct GPU blits and CPU chroma bytes, but a read from
+        // the aliased image changed 559 to 656 U/V samples per frame. An
+        // ordinary private image copied from the same bytes, or the texel-row
+        // binding, reads them all exactly. Such a sampled alias is therefore
+        // not a proven in-place representation. Refuse only this plane and
+        // memory shape; the existing shadow route offers direct texel-buffer
+        // reads without copies for eligible shader slots.
+        // An alternative DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR image imported from the
+        // exported DMA-BUF is still an image alias of the same chroma plane.
+        // Reject that alternative too: the shader-visible image representation
+        // is what failed, not the contents or the ability to import the bytes.
+        // The caller can select direct texel-buffer rows (for eligible shader
